From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Settings ordered by what one wants to do

The panel list had grown along the components: 25 rows in five groups
without names, and the same subject in several places. Now it has named
sections (Connections, Phone, Apps, Security, System) and 22 rows:

- Hubs: USB, Streaming, Printers, Mouse and Graphics Tablets are
  rows on Connected Devices, Your Account and Online Accounts on
  Accounts, the assistant button on Keyboard & Buttons. They stay real
  panels: search finds them, "gnome-control-center usb" and the quick
  settings open them on top of their hub, with their parameters. A
  panel opened that way is a static subpage of the hub, which GNOME's
  shell can already do; it gets its title and parameters there, and is
  cancelled when popped.
- Lock & Unlock: the ways to unlock from the user page and the lock
  options from the Screen Lock page on one page. The user page shows
  a section of its rows, the Screen Lock page hands over its groups.
- Privacy and Security apart: Security is a panel of its own with the
  phone's checks that were "Device Security" in Privacy & Security,
  and the encryption page; Privacy keeps location, cameras, file
  history and diagnostics.
- Secure Shell has left System for Remote Access (the VNC panel).
- Automatic brightness, dimming and the screen-off delay are on Display
  only; the delay was on Power and on Screen Lock.
- The mouse panel only shows with a mouse or touchpad.

What belongs where is in shell/cc-plinius-hubs.c, the phone's names for
GNOME's panels in shell/cc-panel-loader.c.
---
diff --git a/panels/hubs/meson.build b/panels/hubs/meson.build
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f654fea
--- /dev/null
+++ b/panels/hubs/meson.build
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Plinius: the panels that are nothing but rows to other panels. The sources and the desktop files
+# (with their translations) come as separate files of gnome-control-center-plinius.
+panels_list += [ 'connected-devices', 'accounts' ]
+
+install_data(
+  'gnome-connected-devices-panel.desktop',
+  'gnome-accounts-panel.desktop',
+  install_dir: control_center_desktopdir,
+)
+
+sources = files(
+  'cc-plinius-hub-panels.c',
+)
+
+panels_libs += static_library(
+  cappletname,
+  sources: sources,
+  include_directories: [ top_inc, common_inc ],
+  dependencies: common_deps,
+  c_args: cflags,
+)
